cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use cosmet, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "cosmet: Analysis of Ecotoxicological Mesocosm Experiments"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/STABLE-uv/cosmet"
authors:
  - family-names: "Amador Crespo"
    given-names: "Pablo"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3793-8794"
  - family-names: "Rico"
    given-names: "Andreu"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1820-4218"
abstract: >-
  R package for the classic analysis of aquatic mesocosm and microcosm
  experiments with chemicals: validation of the design, Williams' and
  Dunnett's tests of every treatment against the control by taxon and
  sampling date, no observed effect concentrations with criteria for
  consistent effects, minimum detectable differences, and principal response
  curves with their permutation tests.
keywords:
  - R
  - ecotoxicology
  - mesocosms
  - NOEC
  - principal response curves
  - Williams test
